WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.467
Step 1. Open the specimen definitions list. Here you change a specimen definition,

1.2
00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:10.030
or retire one that the facility no longer uses.

1.3
00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:14.851
In Settings, under Clinical, select Specimen Definitions.

2.1
00:00:14.851 --> 00:00:17.953
Step 2. Update the specimen definition.

2.2
00:00:17.953 --> 00:00:22.268
Select Edit in its row, change the fields, and select Save.

2.3
00:00:22.268 --> 00:00:30.445
When you change the title, Care does not change the slug.

3.1
00:00:30.445 --> 00:00:33.617
Step 3. Retire the specimen definition.

3.2
00:00:33.617 --> 00:00:39.837
Select View in its row, then Delete, then Confirm. Care sets its status to Retired,

3.3
00:00:39.837 --> 00:00:44.308
and the activity definition form no longer offers it.

4.1
00:00:44.308 --> 00:00:48.909
Step 4. Make a retired specimen definition Active again.

4.2
00:00:48.909 --> 00:00:51.783
In the Status filter, select Retired.

4.3
00:00:51.783 --> 00:00:55.745
Select Edit, set Status to Active, and select Save.

4.4
00:00:55.745 --> 00:00:59.742
The activity definition form offers it again.
